@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To OSB Team Role Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki team role integration to OSB and Project Details works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oneiki - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| OSB Devlopr Team |
	| OSB Mktng Team   |
	* I tear down the team roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Role  |
	| NonLiferay Accnt Role |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create team role
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a team role on Koroneiki that later gets synced to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a team with the name "OSB Devlopr Team" for the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I assign the team with the name "OSB Devlopr Team" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Team" and "OSB Devlopr Team" with the field value "Team Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Team                 |
	| Update Description          | OSB Devlopr Team              |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Team Role                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Account Role          |

Scenario: Create team role executed by agent
	Testing the ability to create a team role executed by agent on Koroneiki that later gets synced to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a team with the name "OSB Devlopr Team" for the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I assign the team with the name "OSB Devlopr Team" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles executed by "Koroneiki User"
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Team" and "OSB Devlopr Team" with the field value "Team Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User       |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Team        |
	| Update Description          | OSB Devlopr Team     |
	| Update Date                 | Today                |
	| Update Field Name           | Team Role            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Account Role |

